  "body": "### Summary\nLOT-140 (#230) must notify a new reply in an MP conversation that is already unread. The home count does not change in that case. We need two captures of the MP list page 1 to see what changes on the row.\n\n### Capture\n1. Have a test account receive an MP and leave it unread. Capture the MP list page 1 (`HFREndpoint.privateMessages`, logged in).\n2. Have the other party reply once more, without opening the conversation. Capture the same page again.\n3. Optional: a third reply, and a group MP doing the same.\n\n### What to record\nOn the same row, before and after:\n- `repliesCount`;\n- `lastPost` (date and author);\n- the unread icon (`closedbp`);\n- the order of the rows.\n\nDoes the row stay `isUnread`?\n\nAnonymize per FIXTURES.md: no real pseudo, cookie or token. Add the pages next to `R13u1` with the next free ids, and record the facts under LOT-140's `###` subsection in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c.\n\n### Wanted by\n- LOT-140 (#230), for reply detection.\n- The LOT-091 ledger follow-up.",
